// RobotWin Studio Setup: one installer for every kind of installation. Native Win32, nothing to install first.
//
// The setup carries no application. It carries the list of its release's components (components.h, generated by
// tools/build-installer.ps1: file name, size, SHA-256, size on disk) and takes the chosen ones from the release on
// GitHub, from a folder (the one it is in, for an offline install, or /SOURCE=<folder>) or from a mirror
// (/SOURCE=<url>). Every file is checked against its SHA-256 before anything in the installation changes; a broken
// download goes on where it stopped.
//
// Kinds (the first page, or /TYPE=):
//   full     the app, its own .NET 9 runtime, the Arduino compiler and STEP / IGES support: everything works offline
//   lite     the app alone, on the PC's .NET 9 Desktop Runtime (its own copy only when the PC has none)
//   custom   any set of components (/COMPONENTS=app,dotnet,arduino,occt)
// Where: this user (default), all users (/ALLUSERS, elevated) or portable (/PORTABLE: a folder only, no shortcuts,
// no registry, no file types). The language chosen on the first page is the app's language too.
//
//   setup.exe                                  the wizard
//   setup.exe /S | /PASSIVE                    silent | progress window only (the in-app updater)
//       [/TYPE=full|lite|custom] [/COMPONENTS=...] [/LANG=en|tr] [/D=<dir>] [/ALLUSERS] [/PORTABLE]
//       [/NODESKTOP] [/NOTYPES] [/LAUNCH] [/SOURCE=<url or folder>] [/KEEP]
//   setup.exe --pack <dir> <out.rwpack>        build time: packs a component's folder
//   Uninstall.exe [/S]                         removes the installation (the setup copies itself there)
//   Uninstall.exe /MODIFY                      the wizard on the installed copy: add or remove components
//
// An install into an existing folder keeps its kind, components and language unless told otherwise, and removes the
// files of the previous installation that the new one does not have (install.log). install.json records what was
// installed; the app reads it (its language is the default of users who have no settings yet).
//
// .rwpack: "RWPACK01", u32 count, then per file { u16 n, wchar path[n], u64 size, u64 stored, byte data[stored] };
// stored < size: LZMS (Windows Compression API), stored == size: as is.

